00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:02.260
And this is probably good human being advice

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:05.160
Not just an entrepreneur and startup and investor advice

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:06.780
The true story of Wine Library TV was

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:08.680
The day that I thought I was going to start it

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:11.489
I thought I was going to do something similar to QVC

00:00:11.489 --> 00:00:14.820
And I I don't know if you have a QVC or shopping network in Europe

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:17.760
But QVC in America is a show and they sell stuff through the TV

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:20.320
I thought I was going to do the QVC of wine

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:23.560
The first episode of that show

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:25.060
When that camera went on

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:26.480
and that light went on

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:29.400
I realized that this was going to be on the internet forever

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:31.940
And that I didn't want to just Peddle wine

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:37.040
I decided I wanted to be a value to people in learning about wine

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:40.640
Because I was scared that if I was peddling something I didn't believe in

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:41.960
that somebody would come up to me at a party

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:42.840
and say do you like this

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:43.924
and I'd say no I hate it.

00:00:43.924 --> 00:00:46.600
They're like well, you fucking said it was awesome on WineLibrary TV

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:47.600
You're a scam artist!

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:48.760
I'm like "Shit! No!"

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:49.700
So

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:51.960
I was very focused on leveling up

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:54.720
and I really believe the one great piece of advice

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:57.240
If you want to take anything from this talk is

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:58.700
We have to start realizing

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:01.890
that giving and doing things in business

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:05.560
without expectation of return

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:07.060
From the other individual

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:09.100
is probably the greatest leverage

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:11.360
that you could ever deploy in your business life

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:15.660
though it is extremely rare in today's business environment

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:17.700
and it has absolutely been the Bedrock

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:19.140
of what has allowed me to win

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:20.660
All my engagement

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:22.280
all my selfies right over there

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:23.140
and signing books

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:24.330
all the content

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:25.900
I have nothing to sell

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:29.800
I have a book that I fucking sell once every three years for Thirteen dollars

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:32.220
This is not about monetizing an audience

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:35.260
it's about building leverage to build brand

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:37.400
versus sales

